  "notes": [
    "Ranges are half-open and addresses are decimal.",
    "Zero-page ranges are hexadecimal; union of declared fixed cells, allocated homes and mapped source storage. Implicit runtime/emitter scratch is not a separate allocation census.",
    "Final image hash/size includes XEX framing. image_span_bytes is the emitter byte span; reserved ranges are reported separately and retain their sizes while moving with code.",
    "Cycles include the common call wrapper. Print cycles use deterministic RTS output stubs; no screen or disk I/O timing is included.",
    "All six feature-off baseline images match the frozen manifest byte for byte.",
    "Samples without candidate sites keep their prior lowering; this extension covers unsigned BYTE <= and > with an adjacent indirect RHS load."
  ],
